---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { accessProfiles, accessFaqs, accessibilitySources as sources, accessibilityReviewedAt } from '../data/accessibilityPlanning';
---
<BaseLayout title="Accessible Banff: Trail Profiles, Transport & Visitor Access" description="Plan Banff with published trail widths, slopes and surfaces, attraction access features, mobility transport questions and adaptive activity resources." lastUpdated={accessibilityReviewedAt}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({ '@context':'https://schema.org', '@type':'FAQPage', mainEntity:accessFaqs.map(faq => ({ '@type':'Question', name:faq.question, acceptedAnswer:{ '@type':'Answer', text:faq.answer } })) })} />
  <div class="container"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label:'Accessible Banff' }]} /></div>
  <section class="page-hero"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1464822759023-fed622ff2c3b?w=1600&q=80" alt="Mountain landscape" class="page-hero-bg" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" /><div class="page-hero-content"><span class="badge">Plan Your Visit</span><h1>Accessible Banff: Build Your Outing</h1><p>Choose the experience, compare its actual access features and make the journey work for your group.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container access-page">
    <div class="intro"><h2>Start with what makes a good day for you</h2><p>A lake view, a forest outing, an exhibition and a summit-building visit involve different surfaces and journeys. Pick one main experience, include time to rest, and arrange the return with the outward trip. A short visit can be the whole plan.</p><p>For the whole visit, read the <a href="/blog/accessible-banff/">arrival, room and assistance guide</a>. For a specific outing, use <a href="/blog/banff-accessible-hikes/">outdoor viewpoints and complete returns</a>.</p><p>Use the published features to prepare questions about your wheelchair, scooter, stroller or other access needs. Confirm current works, weather, washrooms and assistance with the operator before committing.</p><nav aria-label="Accessibility guide sections"><a href="#trail-profiles">Trail profiles</a><a href="#places">Places to visit</a><a href="#transport">Transport</a><a href="#support">Support and equipment</a><a href="#stay">Room planning</a></nav></div>
    <h2 id="trail-profiles">Compare the physical trail profiles</h2><p>Figures come from <a href={sources.trails} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Parks Canada's hiking profiles ↗</a>. Width is <strong>typical / minimum</strong>; grade and cross slope are <strong>typical / maximum</strong>. Cross slope is the sideways tilt. A small typical figure can coexist with a short, steep or narrow section.</p>
    <form id="profile-comparison" class="compare-controls" aria-label="Compare two trail profiles" hidden><div><label for="profile-a">First profile</label><select id="profile-a">{accessProfiles.map(profile => <option value={profile.id}>{profile.name}</option>)}</select></div><div><label for="profile-b">Second profile</label><select id="profile-b">{accessProfiles.map((profile,i) => <option value={profile.id} selected={i === 1}>{profile.name}</option>)}</select></div><button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary" id="profile-compare">Compare selected profiles</button><button type="button" class="btn btn-outline" id="profile-reset">Show all profiles</button></form>
    <p id="profile-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">All three published profiles are shown.</p><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Physical trail profile comparison"><table id="access-table"><caption>Published route measurements; not current access reports</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Feature</th>{accessProfiles.map(profile => <th scope="col" data-profile={profile.id}>{profile.name}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Stated distance</th>{accessProfiles.map(profile => <td data-profile={profile.id}>{profile.distance}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Surface mix</th>{accessProfiles.map(profile => <td data-profile={profile.id}>{profile.surface}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Width: typical / minimum</th>{accessProfiles.map(profile => <td data-profile={profile.id}>{profile.width}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Grade: typical / maximum</th>{accessProfiles.map(profile => <td data-profile={profile.id}>{profile.grade}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Cross slope: typical / maximum</th>{accessProfiles.map(profile => <td data-profile={profile.id}>{profile.crossSlope}</td>)}</tr><tr><th scope="row">Obstacles to investigate</th>{accessProfiles.map(profile => <td data-profile={profile.id}>{profile.obstacle}</td>)}</tr>
    </tbody></table></div><noscript><p>The complete comparison and all planning notes are available without JavaScript.</p></noscript><div class="access-sections">{accessProfiles.map(profile => <article class="access-entry"><h3>{profile.name}</h3><p>{profile.approach}</p><a href={sources.report} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Current trail report ↗</a></article>)}</div>
    <div class="notice"><h3>Snow season needs a separate decision</h3><p>The profiles describe published routes, not cleared winter paths. Snow can hide edges and obstacles; ice changes slopes and braking. Check <a href={sources.report} target="_blank" rel="noopener">trail reports</a> and <a href={sources.bulletins} target="_blank" rel="noopener">closures</a>, discuss the approach with Parks, and keep an alternative near your base. Equipment does not override a closure.</p><p><strong>Johnston Canyon, checked October 29, 2026:</strong> the main canyon approach is closed for construction, with a scheduled end of December 11. That date is not confirmation of reopening. The <a href="/blog/johnston-canyon-guide">Johnston Canyon guide</a> separates the closure, endpoints and transport.</p></div>
    <h2 id="places">Build a visit around a specific place</h2><div class="access-sections">
      <article class="access-entry"><h3>Cave and Basin history visit</h3><p>Parks lists accessible parking, ramps and an elevator, and an accessible indoor/outdoor introductory tour. It is an exhibition visit, with no bathing. Confirm the route and facilities for your date; building features do not establish access on every surrounding boardwalk.</p><p><a href="https://parks.canada.ca/lhn-nhs/ab/caveandbasin/activ/activites-activities/introduction-basictour" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tour details ↗</a> · <a href="https://parks.canada.ca/voyage-travel/experiences/sources-springs" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Parks access features ↗</a></p></article>
      <article class="access-entry"><h3>Banff Gondola summit building</h3><p>The operator describes assisted cabin loading and elevators serving all four building levels. The published mobility-device size limit is 31 inches wide × 41 inches long, with a total weight limit of 320 kg. Confirm your device, party and loading arrangements.</p><p><strong>The outdoor summit boardwalk has 368 shallow stairs each way and is not wheelchair accessible.</strong> A building visit differs from continuing to Sanson's Peak.</p><a href={sources.gondola} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cabin and summit access details ↗</a></article>
      <article class="access-entry"><h3>Upper Hot Springs when operating</h3><p><strong>At the October 29 review, Parks publishes a maintenance closure from October 13 to early November.</strong> Check reopening before arranging a pool visit.</p><p>The facility guide describes an elevator, a ramp alternative to pool-level steps, two accessible changing rooms and aquatic chairs requested at reception. Personal wheelchairs cannot enter the spring water. Confirm elevator dimensions, transfers and available assistance.</p><p><a href="https://parks.canada.ca/pn-np/ab/banff/sources-banff-springs" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Opening notice ↗</a> · <a href={sources.springs} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Facility access guide ↗</a></p></article>
      <article class="access-entry"><h3>A short view rather than a whole trail</h3><p>Banff & Lake Louise Tourism identifies shorter viewing approaches at Lake Louise, Bow Falls, Vermilion Lakes, Bow Lake and summer-only Peyto Lake. Ask about the parking-to-viewpoint journey, slope, washrooms and resting places. A viewpoint listing does not describe the whole trail.</p><p>The <a href="https://www.banff.ca/654/Bow-Falls-Trail" target="_blank" rel="noopener">town's Bow Falls route</a> climbs above the falls; its clifftop section closes in winter. The through-walk and lower viewpoint are separate choices.</p><a href="https://www.banfflakelouise.com/accessibility" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Local access resources ↗</a></article>
    </div>
    <h2 id="transport">Resolve the whole transport chain</h2><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Accessible transport planning"><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Published arrangements</th><th>Confirm for your trip</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Roam Transit</th><td>Ramps, kneeling entrances, priority seating and accessible stop buttons. Some scooters do not fit.</td><td>Device dimensions, boarding stop, final path, space and last return. <a href={sources.roam} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Roam policies ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Reserved Parks lake shuttle</th><td>Accessible vehicle requested at the Lake Louise Park and Ride with a purchased ticket. Moraine has no accessible parking.</td><td>Vehicle, companion and equipment arrangements. The published 2026 season ended October 12; future dates need a new check. The 2026 Alpine Start product had no accessible vehicle. <a href={sources.shuttle} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Parks FAQ ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Hotel or commercial transfer</th><td>The actual operator and vehicle determine arrangements.</td><td>Ramp or lift, securement, party seats, baggage, pickup, return and who provides assistance. Obtain specific confirmation before booking.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>A ramp-equipped bus does not establish access along the final path. Save each leg and contact details offline. Use <a href="/car-free-banff">car-free Banff planning</a> to distinguish town buses, regional routes, lake shuttles and ski services.</p>
    <h2 id="support">Support people, communication and adaptive activities</h2><div class="access-sections"><article class="access-entry"><h3>Parks support-person admission</h3><p>A needed support person accompanying a visitor who depends on that support receives free admission and program access. Parks requires no documentation or Access 2 Card for this policy. It is not a blanket free visitor pass; other admission fees can apply.</p><a href={sources.policy} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Admission policy ↗</a></article><article class="access-entry"><h3>Communication and service animals</h3><p>Parks asks for sign-language or equivalent communication requests at least five business days ahead; availability varies. Service animals are welcome where handlers are permitted, subject to site rules and health, safety or operational limits. Confirm specific arrangements, including pools and transport.</p><a href={sources.policy} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Parks services ↗</a></article><article class="access-entry"><h3>Arrange an adaptive experience</h3><p><a href="https://rockymountainadaptive.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rocky Mountain Adaptive ↗</a> publishes adapted activities, lessons and equipment rentals. Ask about the venue, date, equipment, instructor, support and cancellation terms. Book an actual arrangement rather than assuming equipment is waiting at a visitor centre.</p><p>Combine that conversation with the <a href="/learn-to-ski">lesson planning guide</a>.</p></article></div>
    <h2 id="stay">Book a room category that meets the plan</h2><p>Ask the property to confirm the exact room and bathroom, bed height and clearances, shower or transfer setup, entrance, elevator, parking and equipment. An accessible-room label does not guarantee every feature in every room.</p><p>For one documented example, <a href="https://www.fairmont.com/en/hotels/banff/fairmont-banff-springs.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Fairmont Banff Springs lists a Fairmont Queen Mobility Accessible Roll-in Shower category ↗</a>. Confirm availability and layout directly. Our <a href="/hotel-directory/fairmont-banff-springs">property guide</a> links to Expedia with our existing affiliate tracking; a general search does not reserve an accessible room. We may earn a commission from qualifying bookings.</p>
    <div class="intro"><h3>Keep a practical confirmation list</h3><p>These optional boxes stay on the open page; they do not book services or save personal information.</p><ul class="checklist"><li><label><input type="checkbox" /> I have chosen an endpoint and a return journey.</label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox" /> I have checked narrow passages, steep sections and the current surface.</label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox" /> I have confirmed washrooms, resting places and assistance.</label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox" /> The operator has confirmed my actual equipment and party.</label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox" /> I have an alternative and the relevant contact details.</label></li></ul><p>Use the <a href="/packing-list">packing checklist</a>, <a href="/towns">town comparison</a> and <a href="/winter">winter guide</a> to round out the day.</p></div>
    <h2>Questions visitors ask</h2><div class="faq-list">{accessFaqs.map(faq => <details><summary>{faq.question}</summary><p>{faq.answer}</p></details>)}</div><p class="review-note">Reviewed <time datetime={accessibilityReviewedAt}>October 29, 2026</time> against the linked public sources. Check current operation and individual arrangements with the provider.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
  import { buildAccessComparison } from '../data/accessibilityPlanning';
  const form = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#profile-comparison');
  const first = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#profile-a');
  const second = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#profile-b');
  const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#profile-status');
  if (form && first && second && status) {
    const cells = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('#access-table [data-profile]'));
    const show = (state: ReturnType<typeof buildAccessComparison>) => {
      cells.forEach(cell => { cell.hidden = !state.visibleIds.includes(cell.dataset.profile || ''); });
      status.textContent = state.status;
    };
    const compare = () => show(buildAccessComparison(first.value, second.value));
    form.addEventListener('submit', event => { event.preventDefault(); compare(); });
    [first, second].forEach(field => field.addEventListener('change', compare));
    document.querySelector('#profile-reset')?.addEventListener('click', () => { form.reset(); show(buildAccessComparison()); });
    form.hidden = false;
  }
</script>
<style>
  [hidden] { display:none !important; } .access-page { max-width:1100px; } .access-page p,.access-page li { line-height:1.75; } .access-page p { margin:.7rem 0 1rem; } .access-page h2 { margin:2.5rem 0 1rem; scroll-margin-top:6rem; } .access-page h3 { font-size:1.2rem; margin:.2rem 0 .7rem; } .intro,.notice { padding:1.5rem; border-radius:var(--radius); background:var(--color-bg-alt); margin:1.5rem 0; } .intro h2 { margin-top:0; font-size:1.65rem; line-height:1.3; } .notice { border-left:4px solid #977000; } nav { display:flex; gap:.7rem 1.2rem; flex-wrap:wrap; } .access-sections { margin:1.5rem 0 2.5rem; border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1; } .access-entry { padding:1.5rem 0; border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5e1; display:flow-root; } .access-entry h3 { max-width:23rem; } .access-entry p { max-width:78ch; } @media(min-width:900px) { .access-entry { padding-left:28%; position:relative; } .access-entry h3 { position:absolute; left:0; top:1.6rem; width:24%; } } .review-note { font-size:.85rem; color:var(--color-text-light); } .table-scroll { overflow-x:auto; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius:8px; margin:1.2rem 0; } table { width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; min-width:650px; font-size:.9rem; } caption { text-align:left; padding:.9rem; font-weight:700; background:var(--color-bg-alt); } th,td { padding:.9rem; border-bottom:1px solid #d1d5db; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; } th { background:var(--color-bg-alt); } .compare-controls { display:flex; gap:1rem; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:flex-end; padding:1rem; background:var(--color-bg-alt); border-radius:8px; } .compare-controls>div { display:flex; flex:1 1 220px; flex-direction:column; gap:.4rem; } label { font-weight:600; } select { font:inherit; color:inherit; padding:.7rem; border:1px solid #94a3b8; border-radius:5px; background:white; width:100%; } .checklist { list-style:none; padding:0; } .checklist li { margin:.7rem 0; } .checklist label { display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:.7rem; font-weight:400; } .checklist input { margin-top:.4rem; width:1.15rem; height:1.15rem; flex-shrink:0; } summary { cursor:pointer; font-weight:700; padding:1rem 0; } details { border-bottom:1px solid #d1d5db; } a:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,button:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,.table-scroll:focus-visible { outline:3px solid var(--color-primary); outline-offset:3px; } @media(max-width:600px) { .compare-controls>div { flex-basis:100%; } .intro,.notice { padding:1.1rem; } }
</style>
